course: dictionary
lesson: 7680
title: Prosthetic: a word about people and their bodies
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A prosthetic is an artificial body part, made to replace a part that is missing, such as a leg, arm, hand or eye. Context gives you the clue: «A prosthetic arm or leg is a tool that helps someone, like glasses, so do not stare.» Glasses help people see, so a prosthetic helps a person do things.
explain: Prosthetic can be an adjective, as in a prosthetic leg, or a noun, as in «a prosthetic» or «prosthetics». Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Be respectful. «A disability can be easy to see, like a wheelchair, a white cane or a prosthetic leg, or invisible, like diabetes, a heart problem, autism or ADHD.» Some disabilities can be seen and others cannot, so you cannot tell by looking at someone whether they have one.
fact: Prosthetic means artificial, made to replace a missing body part.
fact: Prosthetic is an adjective in «a prosthetic leg» and a noun in «a prosthetic».
fact: People with a prosthetic leg can walk, run and play sport.
fact: Paralympic athletes use running blades.
fact: The polite thing is to talk to the person, not stare at the prosthetic.
exercise: «A prosthetic arm or leg is a tool that helps someone, like glasses.» What does prosthetic mean? | A sports shoe | *Artificial, made to replace a missing body part | A kind of bandage for a cut | A part of the body that is growing back
exercise: «A disability can be easy to see, like a wheelchair, a white cane or a prosthetic leg, or invisible, like diabetes.» Which one is invisible? | A white cane | *Diabetes | A wheelchair | A prosthetic leg
exercise: A friend has a prosthetic leg. What is the most polite thing to do? | Ask them to take it off so you can look | Stare at the leg to see how it works | Point at it and laugh | *Talk to your friend as you normally would, and do not stare at the prosthetic
test: «Prosthetic arms can help people do everyday tasks.» What part of speech is prosthetic here? | Adverb | Verb | *Adjective | Noun
test: In films, what are prosthetics used for? | Real arms and legs for actors to use | Paint for the walls | Cameras that film at night | *Fake body parts for make-up and effects
exam: A classmate has a prosthetic hand. What is the most respectful response? | Tell the whole class it is fake | Keep asking to see how the hand works | *Treat them the same as anyone else and talk about the person, not the hand | Ask loudly why their hand is different
